      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-09T23:08:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is okay for now, but given that self-tests will need to be added, it would make sense to split this into two patches: one that adds the fips140 module, and one that adds the integrity check to that module.  A third patch later would then add the self-tests to the module.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "8f6855f089f98f225acb301f8b98d04de2f9af7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26720780_be19f876",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-10T14:05:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The module exists because of the integrity selfcheck. Without it, we could put the known-answer selftests in the core kernel (and we could still do so, btw)\n\nSo decoupling the module from the selfcheck does not seem that useful to me, especially given the fact that the peculiar way this module is constructed, in terms of section layout, ordering of operations, etc, exists solely for the purpose of the selfcheck.",
      "parentUuid": "b6cd23a5_98142ea6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "8f6855f089f98f225acb301f8b98d04de2f9af7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
